<title>USA: CIENA to release part of locked up shares.</title>
<headline>CIENA to release part of locked up shares.</headline>
<dateline>LINTHICUM, Md. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>CIENA Corp said on Thursday that Goldman Sachs &amp; Co has agreed to release 10 percent of the 88 million shares that are subject to lock-up agreements due to expire August 7, 1997.</p>
<p>The release, which will be effective May 27, 1997, applies on a pro rata basis to the holdings of each locked up stockholder, CIENA said.</p>
<p>CIENA conducted an initial public offering in February at $23 a share.</p>
<p>CIENA's shares closed at 38-7/8, off 1-1/4, on volume of 667,500 shares.</p>
</text>
